.TH MEDLEN 1 "August 2026" "Medlen 0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
medlen \- report durations and summary statistics for media files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B medlen
[IdirectoryR]
.br
.B medlen
\fB-h\fR | \fB--help\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B medlen
recursively scans a directory for supported media files and prints the duration
of every file it can read. It then prints the total, average, longest, and
shortest durations.
.PP
If no directory is given, the current working directory is scanned. Directory
paths are followed recursively, but symbolic links are not followed by default.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -h, --help
Print usage information and the supported media formats.
.SH SUPPORTED FORMATS
.IP \(bu 2
WAV (\fB.wav\fR)
.IP \(bu 2
MP3 (\fB.mp3\fR)
.IP \(bu 2
FLAC (\fB.flac\fR)
.IP \(bu 2
Ogg Vorbis and Opus (\fB.ogg\fR, \fB.opus\fR)
.IP \(bu 2
MP4 family (\fB.mp4\fR, \fB.m4a\fR, \fB.mov\fR)
.SH OUTPUT
Durations use the format \fIHH:MM:SS.mmm\fR. Unsupported, unreadable, and
malformed files are skipped with warnings and are excluded from the summary.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The scan completed, including when no supported files were found.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command-line arguments or a directory that does not exist.
.SH EXAMPLES
Scan the current directory:
.PP
.EX
medlen
.EE
.PP
Scan a specific directory:
.PP
.EX
medlen /srv/media
.EE
.SH NOTES
Medlen reads container metadata directly and does not require FFmpeg or
MediaInfo. Some unusual containers and variable-bit-rate MP3 files may not
provide an exact duration.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR apt (8)
